WEBVTT


00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.271
I want to tell the people


00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.034
of Barcelona, of Catalonia,


00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.839
that I really thank you


00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.197
for the warm welcome
you've given our army.


00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.469
I'd also like the Spaniards to know
that it was a big mistake


00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.279
to think that Catalans
were separatists,


00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.829
and were against Spain.


00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.476
I must say we have received


00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.551
the most enthusiast welcome


00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.630
I've ever seen,


00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.429
and I have been lucky enough


00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.750
to attend similar acts.


00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.717
Nowhere, I tell you,


00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.518
nowhere have we been received


00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.150
with as much enthusiasm
and friendliness as in Barcelona.


00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.953
BARCELONA (A MAP)


00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:16.029
Have you come
to ask me to go again?


00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.192
Actually, I've come to beg you
to leave.


00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.069
Come in.


00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.156
I wish I could give you something


00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.356
worthy of your patience.


00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.069
No, you don't owe me anything.


00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.639
I'm sick and I can't afford
to pretend what I don't feel.


00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.037
You can afford to be honest.


00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.839
That's a very wild luxury.


00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.790
What can I give you


00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.989
that's worthy of you?


00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.829
I know.


00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.148
This photograph.


00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:03.316
Come in.


00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.231
Who is it? I don't know him.


00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:21.469
Juan Rubio.


00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:25.793
This picture was taken
as he danced over his mother's body.


00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.998
After he'd killed her.


00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.356
Why?


00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.514
Why?


00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.394
He was crazy, or lucid, who knows.


00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.399
It was in the tabloids
a long time ago.


00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:39.709
It's a gift.


00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.149
I don't want it.


00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.470
Don't reject my gift.


00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.517
It's my only luxury.


00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.149
Are you going to go?


00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:57.313
I've always left before being asked.
I'm growing old.


00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:01.599
Can I sit down?


00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.279
How come we've never really talked?


00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.910
People only really talk
when they're about to die,


00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.469
and it's not usually interesting.


00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.479
Are we really talking now?


00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.079
I guess so.


00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:27.909
Why can we today?


00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:31.671
I have nothing to lose
and you're dying.


00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.275
- Do you think I'm pitiful?
- No.


00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.318
And do you think I am pitiful?


00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.036
No.


00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.714
This moment needs music.


00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.071
Let's see if we get lucky.


00:05:58.640 --> 00:05:59.516
<i>La Bohème.</i>


00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:01.116
Do you know it?


00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.753
I was a doorman at the Opera
for 35 years.


00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.798
I retired the year it was burnt.


00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.397
You must know who did it.


00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.838
I wasn't there that day.


00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.000
Isn't it weird that nobody was?


00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:24.749
I don't know.


00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.992
I don't like looking back.


00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.715
I don't like looking forwards.


00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.519
Is that why you hide?


00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.035
I hide?


00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.239
You hardly go out,


00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.790
and if you do, it's at night.


00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.830
Cities are more bearable
at night.


00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.389
I take walks.


00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.192
Sometimes I stop in front
of the buildings my son built.


00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.237
I look for the open windows
which are lit


00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.312
and watch the inhabitants
for a while.


00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:07.872
No architect is brave enough
to do something like that.


00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.314
Not even my son.


00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:21.198
I can't sleep at night.


00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.518
I'm scared of dying while sleeping.


00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.997
And I dream a lot.


00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.037
Lately I dream of the war.


00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.153
The day the war finished, mostly.


00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.231
Wars never finish, Ramon.


00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.710
They just go on one after the other,
but don't finish.


00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.878
Why did you turn it off?


00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.032
When Callas sings,
nobody should talk.


00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.511
Did you know I met her?


00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:59.196
The year I started working
at the 0pera.


00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:04.393
An admirer gave her a puppy
and it ran away in the Rambles.


00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.428
She was desperate
when she got to the 0pera


00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:10.359
and made me promise I'd find it.


00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.231
I looked for it for over 2 hours,
but couldn't find it.


00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:18.350
I shut myself in a closet
until she was gone.


00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:20.638
I didn't want her to see me.


00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:25.148
I can't stand disappointing people.


00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:26.514
And me?


00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:31.037
Doesn't it bother you to kick me out
after so long?


00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:38.279
My wife and I want to spend
my last months on our own.


00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:41.559
If I leave now,
I'll lose my last students.


00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.279
You'll find more.


00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:45.034
Don't be so sure.


00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:49.633
People have lost faith in French
and God to the same extent.


00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.190
If someone prays,
they do it in English now,


00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:54.596
didn't you know?


00:08:56.240 --> 00:09:00.233
I stopped believing in God
during the war, hearing the bombs.


00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:03.639
The more the ruins,
the less I believed.


00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.710
Praying would be hypocritical.


00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.793
Why don't you teach English?


00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.990
I'm not good enough
and I dislike it.


00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:19.999
French...


00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.790
French is very different.


00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.718
I've even taught French in bars,


00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.190
when I had lots of students
and bars were a part of life,


00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.112
not only somewhere


00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:35.953
to drink and spend time.


00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:42.075
I'm sorry I've never smoked


00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.354
or drunk.


00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:49.035
Something to blame my illness on.


00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.151
I can't blame anyone.


00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:57.390
Everyone I knew has died.


00:09:57.880 --> 00:09:59.916
There's only my wife left.


00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:01.790
Do you love her?


00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:04.072
Rosa? Yes, very much.


00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:12.191
Actually, when I met her
I was a bit scared of her.


00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:13.951
Scared?


00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:17.319
I'm glad I'm going to die
before her.


00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:19.038
Alone, I wouldn't know
what to do.


00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.069
And you must love Barcelona.


00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.395
Yes, of course.


00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.517
I've always lived here.


00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.273
Sorry. The doctor told me
not to hold in farts or belches.


00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:43.439
I need to know when you're leaving.
I need to know tonight.


00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.394
It isn't easy to find
a place like this.


00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.752
There are many rooms for rent.


00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:51.718
Not where I can teach too.


00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:55.394
And I want one with an lift.


00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:00.153
That will give my students
one less reason not to learn French.


00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:02.234
Why don't you rent a flat?


00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.873
Can you imagine all this mess
in a whole flat?


00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.154
No, this is enough for me.


00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.436
Can't you stay with your son?


00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:15.434
My son and I can't stand each other
for more than an hour.


00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:20.476
I made the mistake of being
totally honest with him


00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:23.230
and not hiding my faults.


00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:26.159
He never forgave me.


00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:33.114
The only thing we've got in common


00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:37.159
is we feel like shouting when
we're in front of Sagrada Família.


00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:50.075
Don't you like it?


00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.750
You should ask.


00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.514
If the Sagrada Família like us?


00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.989
If I were it, I'd scream too


00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:03.153
with all that's around me
and no way of escaping.


00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.468
You could leave Barcelona.


00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:11.828
I've been away for long periods,
but I always come back.


00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:16.353
It's similar to any other
Western capital,


00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:19.398
content and happy with itself.


00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:23.637
If you like, I can help you
pack all this up.


00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:27.230
No, I think I'll throw it all away.


00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.757
The magazines too?


00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.909
Every time I move, I say I'll throw
everything away, but I don't.


00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.592
<i>Nasti de Plasti.</i>


00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.116
Do you want it?


00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:40.635
No.


00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.875
I've never liked anything
enough to keep it.


00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:48.875
My wife does. She's kept
a diary since she was a child.


00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:53.439
After we got married,
she let me read it,


00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:56.748
but I said it wasn't necessary.


00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:00.597
She's never spoke of it since.


00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:03.320
I wrote a book a long time ago.


00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:07.795
Back then everybody wrote a book,
just one,


00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:12.393
and then spent years saying
how difficult it was to write.


00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.631
What kind of book? A novel?


00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:18.950
A novel that's out of print,


00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:21.315
as all the ideas it contained.


00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:24.956
I wanted to write about ideas,
not feelings,


00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.630
but people have always
preferred feelings.


00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.111
And they're right.


00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:35.037
Ideas end up expiring.


00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:39.189
Feelings, even if they're pathetic,
never expire.


00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:40.919
You don't write anymore?


00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:44.995
My best quality is
to always retire on time.


00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.071
I could give you a plot.


00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:55.633
For a novel?


00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.473
But you must promise not to
publish it before my wife dies.


00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.870
It's interesting.


00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:17.319
No, forget it.
It's silly. It wouldn't work.


00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:19.436
- What?
- It doesn't matter.


00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:21.908
You won't tell me.


00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:24.711
No.


00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:26.956
What a shame.


00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:30.430
I've not heard anything
interesting in ages.


00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:33.114
Everyone I know is too busy


00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.713
to live something interesting.


00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.671
And your students?


00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:40.070
They're the busiest.


00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:44.753
They want to learn enough French
to read travel guides


00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:47.912
and expensive restaurant menus
in Paris


00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:50.071
or Shanghai.


00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.838
You shouldn't scold them.


00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.234
Scold them?


00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:56.675
Sometimes I hear you
from the sitting room.


00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.394
What do you hear?


00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.119
How you scold them.


00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.632
I don't scold them,
we discuss things.


00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:09.350
Some are my friends' children,


00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:14.674
the ones I ran to Paris with


00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.833
without any money
but lots of ideas.


00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.952
Molière, Montaigne,
Voltaire, Diderot...


00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:24.430
The first thing they want to learn
is the word <i>merde</i>,


00:15:24.600 --> 00:15:28.593
but they're not interested
in when to use it.


00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.759
That's why we argue.


00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:33.918
You can't simply shout "<i>merde</i>"


00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.149
when you step on a dog's turd.


00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:44.039
I can't speak languages
and haven't travelled far.


00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:46.155
I envy you.


00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:47.839
Me? Why?


00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.200
You can fart wherever you want.


00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.790
I wouldn't if it wasn't
for the doctor.


00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:02.269
Come with me tonight.


00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:04.192
- Where?
- For a walk.


00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.351
- For a walk?
- For a while.


00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:09.675
- No, it's late.
- Just a little while.


00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:14.990
- Why do you want me to go for a walk?
- Nothing in particular.


00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.358
You find reasons to walk
while walking.


00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.194
I walk very slowly and soon
get tired. We won't go far.


00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:24.270
It doesn't matter.


00:16:24.560 --> 00:16:27.028
I can't climb stairs,


00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:30.316
and I don't want
to leave my wife alone.


00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.836
<i>Voici le soir charmant,</i>
<i>ami du criminel.</i>


00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:38.349
I have the feeling everything
I say lately, I've read somewhere.


00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.352
I never read much.


00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.835
I left school early to start working.


00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.036
At the Opera?


00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.395
No. That was later.


00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:49.038
You must've heard a lot of operas.


00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.831
Some bits. None completely.


00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:56.389
- You have a good ear, then.
- Why?


00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:58.198
You recognized <i>La Bohème.</i>


00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.990
I didn't.


00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:05.629
My wife said
it would be on the radio.


00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.077
- Rosa does like opera.
- You don't?


00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:14.591
When I met her I told her I did


00:17:16.880 --> 00:17:20.270
and after getting married
I didn't dare tell her the truth.


00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.353
And it's too late now.


00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:26.354
Too late?


00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.077
To tell her the truth.


00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:31.589
I don't know.


00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:35.552
I've never known
when to bite my tongue.


00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.880
That's why I'm not invited anywhere.


00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:41.315
From time to time
a divorced friend calls,


00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.277
or someone feeling nostalgic.


00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:46.830
I don't see anyone because
I don't want to pity them,


00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:49.719
or worse, having them pity me.


00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:53.396
Well...


00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.197
Are you leaving tomorrow, then?


00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.309
So soon?


00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:01.434
Monday, then.


00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.233
Monday...


00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.391
It can't be after Monday.


00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:10.873
<i>Avalanche, veux-tu m'emporter</i>
<i>dans ta chute?</i>


00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:21.070
I'll help you pack everything,
if you want,


00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:25.593
but remember to tell your students
not to come back here.


00:18:26.640 --> 00:18:29.518
I think I'll ask them to go
and I'll spend some time


00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.992
translating cookery and DIY books.


00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.515
But I'll go back to French.
In the end, it's only vanity.


00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.432
I like myself much better
when teaching French.


00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.956
It's a photogenic matter.
It's like Juan Rubio.


00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:49.152
I'm sure he was never


00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:50.799
as photogenic as there,


00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.472
dancing naked
over his mother's corpse.


00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.431
Why did he undress completely?


00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.876
To feel more authentic.


00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.519
More authentic?


00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.637
Isn't that
what getting undressed is?


00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:06.310
I don't know.


00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.669
Haven't you ever felt
the need to get undressed


00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.917
just to be really looked at?


00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.479
I don't think so.


00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:30.360
Sometimes, at the Opera,


00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.191
I hid and disguised myself.


00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:38.830
I liked going
to the costume storeroom


00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:40.759
and trying things on.


00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:43.992
There were all sorts of clothes,
from every period.


00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:47.039
If I'd been discovered,
they'd have fired me.


00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.272
- Nobody ever saw you disguised?
- No.


00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:53.390
Would you have liked so?


00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.513
I don't think so.


00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:20.671
Yes?


00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:22.872
Can I come in, David?


00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:24.629
Just a minute.


00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:35.276
Come in.


00:22:40.760 --> 00:22:42.352
Aren't you going out tonight?


00:22:42.520 --> 00:22:43.316
No.


00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:47.034
- My knee hurts.
- What's wrong?


00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:49.949
I have to be x-rayed on Monday.


00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:52.156
- Can't you play on Sunday?
- No.


00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:57.591
- How did you get hurt?
- Running, on my own.


00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:01.275
- Does it hurt?
- A little.


00:23:02.640 --> 00:23:05.598
- Did you call your boss?
- Not yet.


00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:16.433
Did you tell them you're moving
on Monday?


00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:20.674
I can't leave on Monday.
I'll have to wait


00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:22.512
till I find someone
to lend a hand.


00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:25.274
- When are you leaving, then?
- I don't know.


00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:27.676
Maybe next Friday.


00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:28.590
Maybe?


00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:30.796
There's a lot of stairs to climb.


00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:36.909
It makes me nervous to have
a gun in the house.


00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:40.631
- It's unloaded.
- That doesn't make a difference.


00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:53.596
- Won't they miss the gun?
- I'll take it back.


00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:55.917
Aren't you afraid they'll fire you?


00:23:56.240 --> 00:23:58.151
I'll probably leave before.


00:23:58.320 --> 00:24:01.551
They're short of staff,
but don't pay well.


00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:04.997
Why don't you call your wife?


00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:07.835
My wife?


00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:10.355
She might help you move.


00:24:10.560 --> 00:24:14.553
We haven't talked in a long time.
She's with someone else.


00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:22.668
Ataxi driver.


00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:26.798
I thought I might catch his cab,


00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:28.839
have him drive and


00:24:29.000 --> 00:24:32.595
instead of paying him, pulling
the gun out and scaring him some.


00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:33.871
Get out.


00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:36.355
- What you doing?
- Get the fuck out!


00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:40.474
Are you crazy?
What are you doing?


00:24:41.320 --> 00:24:44.676
Shut up you cunt!


00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:55.389
- Were you going to do it tonight?
- No, not tonight.


00:24:59.760 --> 00:25:00.715
And the volume?


00:25:01.360 --> 00:25:02.588
I turned it off.


00:25:03.120 --> 00:25:04.712
It's Barça, isn't it?


00:25:06.200 --> 00:25:07.997
It's an old game.


00:25:08.960 --> 00:25:12.350
I cant' stand commentators,
they know nothing about football.


00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:16.234
I can't see you.


00:25:16.680 --> 00:25:17.510
Who?


00:25:18.480 --> 00:25:19.549
Aren't you playing?


00:25:19.720 --> 00:25:22.314
I never made the first team.


00:25:23.800 --> 00:25:27.793
We both said we'd go and see
you play, but we haven't yet.


00:25:28.240 --> 00:25:29.798
You play for Europa FC, right?


00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:31.951
No. Júpiter.


00:25:32.120 --> 00:25:33.838
Júpiter.


00:25:35.280 --> 00:25:36.918
I won't forget, now.


00:25:40.400 --> 00:25:43.995
Your room's very tidy.
I've never seen it like this.


00:25:44.800 --> 00:25:47.189
Did you hear all the noise today?


00:25:47.680 --> 00:25:51.275
When it's not Gaudí year,
it's Dalí, or something else.


00:25:52.560 --> 00:25:54.596
So much noise makes me nervous.


00:25:57.560 --> 00:26:01.553
You know, I've never been
to the top of the Sagrada Família.


00:26:03.680 --> 00:26:07.275
I haven't been to a museum
or an exhibit in years.


00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:13.155
When I was young, museums were empty,
there weren't any guards,


00:26:13.320 --> 00:26:17.108
anyone could steal a picture
and bring it home.


00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:21.158
- Most museums are still empty.
- Really?


00:26:21.560 --> 00:26:24.552
People would rather rob
a shopping mall.


00:26:24.720 --> 00:26:26.312
That's where most people go.


00:26:26.480 --> 00:26:28.948
Do you work at a mall?


00:26:29.120 --> 00:26:30.109
I keep changing.


00:26:30.280 --> 00:26:33.033
- Do you have a lot of work?
- Too much.


00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:36.789
The richer the rich get, the more
scared they are of being robbed.


00:26:40.200 --> 00:26:41.599
Did you see my husband?


00:26:41.760 --> 00:26:43.910
Yesterday. We talked.


00:26:44.080 --> 00:26:45.149
What did he say?


00:26:45.320 --> 00:26:48.551
He asked when I was leaving.
Three times.


00:26:53.520 --> 00:26:56.432
- I went to a bullfight today.
- What?


00:26:56.600 --> 00:27:00.070
I used to date a boy who liked it,
and took me to see them.


00:27:00.240 --> 00:27:03.312
I never told my parents,
they wouldn't have let me.


00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.232
I'd never been back till today.


00:27:18.440 --> 00:27:21.159
- Did you like it?
- Not at all.


00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:23.956
I left before it was over.


00:27:24.160 --> 00:27:26.151
It's natural they're closing down.


00:27:28.440 --> 00:27:32.319
Have you ever stopped doing something
for no reason?


00:27:34.320 --> 00:27:38.233
Such as forgetting were
you stopped reading,


00:27:38.400 --> 00:27:40.197
and never picking the book up again.


00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:45.919
If I'd had sisters, I could see
how they're doing,


00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:50.837
and know if I've been wrong or not.


00:27:52.600 --> 00:27:55.068
I've never missed
not having brothers.


00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:58.792
My father wanted a boy badly,


00:27:59.160 --> 00:28:02.630
and when he saw I was a girl,
he completely ignored me


00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:05.394
and hid in his factory.


00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:09.040
For years, as a little girl,


00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:13.359
I wanted to be a boy
for his sake,


00:28:14.480 --> 00:28:17.278
and when I accepted
I'd never be one,


00:28:18.320 --> 00:28:21.073
I dreamt someone
would burn the factory down


00:28:21.240 --> 00:28:24.232
and my father would pay
some attention to me.


00:28:30.440 --> 00:28:32.351
Then my brother was born.


00:28:37.760 --> 00:28:39.159
And your mother?


00:28:39.960 --> 00:28:42.554
She was completely useless.


00:28:44.040 --> 00:28:46.759
When she got married,
she disappeared.


00:28:47.920 --> 00:28:50.753
She walked around the house
afraid of stepping on the floor.


00:28:50.920 --> 00:28:54.469
She did everything my father said
and soon I didn't respect her.


00:28:55.400 --> 00:28:57.709
People only respect what they fear.


00:28:59.280 --> 00:29:02.477
You can also respect
what you admire.


00:29:03.040 --> 00:29:05.429
- Did you admire your father?
- No.


00:29:07.160 --> 00:29:08.434
I just loved him.


00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:11.518
I've only admired some
football players,


00:29:12.120 --> 00:29:13.439
but not anymore.


00:29:14.040 --> 00:29:17.476
- Football is getting boring.
- Why do you watch it, then?


00:29:18.040 --> 00:29:20.429
It's the only thing
I know a lot about.


00:29:21.240 --> 00:29:24.994
I know when they're playing well,
who's good and bad.


00:29:25.160 --> 00:29:26.479
Is this match good?


00:29:27.560 --> 00:29:28.788
It's not bad.


00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:32.950
They've edited out the parts,
when nothing happens.


00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:36.437
I wish you could do that with life.


00:29:36.600 --> 00:29:37.749
What?


00:29:37.920 --> 00:29:41.390
Editing out the periods
when nothing interesting happens.


00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:44.910
There would be nothing left.


00:29:45.760 --> 00:29:47.079
How old are you?


00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:49.549
Thirty one.


00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:53.748
I'm 76, but I'd like to be


00:29:54.920 --> 00:29:56.148
40 less.


00:29:56.320 --> 00:29:58.629
36 is the perfect age
for a woman.


00:29:58.800 --> 00:30:01.951
It's not too young
nor too old.


00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:06.595
There's still time to change,
to do something new.


00:30:06.760 --> 00:30:08.432
And for a man?


00:30:08.600 --> 00:30:11.068
I don't know, I'm not a man.


00:30:11.320 --> 00:30:13.788
- I'd say 15.
- So young?


00:30:13.960 --> 00:30:15.552
That was my perfect age.


00:30:16.040 --> 00:30:18.634
It's too early to know.


00:30:22.800 --> 00:30:24.677
What you should do


00:30:25.680 --> 00:30:28.672
is find a job you really like


00:30:28.960 --> 00:30:30.837
and try to keep it.


00:30:31.560 --> 00:30:34.358
I always have the feeling
someone else could do it better.


00:30:34.520 --> 00:30:36.795
There's always someone better.


00:30:37.680 --> 00:30:39.875
In football,
when someone's better,


00:30:40.040 --> 00:30:42.429
he plays and you don't.


00:30:42.840 --> 00:30:44.990
But football is not life.


00:30:45.160 --> 00:30:47.390
That's what my wife said.


00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:52.519
No, she said it the other way round.
Life is not football.


00:30:54.880 --> 00:30:57.030
She's probably with someone
better than me.


00:30:57.200 --> 00:30:58.394
The taxi driver?


00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:00.039
And you.


00:31:00.200 --> 00:31:03.112
Maybe you've found someone better
and you're kicking me out.


00:31:04.760 --> 00:31:06.876
I already told you
you had to leave.


00:31:07.040 --> 00:31:09.634
I could stay in the first room
and you wouldn't see me.


00:31:09.800 --> 00:31:12.268
If you have to hide,
it's not worth staying.


00:31:12.440 --> 00:31:15.273
- You could pretend I'd left.
- I can't pretend I can't see you.


00:31:19.840 --> 00:31:20.909
Who's winning?


00:31:21.080 --> 00:31:23.389
In the old games Barça always wins.


00:31:23.920 --> 00:31:25.911
My father supported Barça.


00:31:27.640 --> 00:31:29.835
He went to the stadium
every Sunday.


00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.709
Even after going bankrupt,
he kept going.


00:31:34.520 --> 00:31:36.829
It was as if nothing had happened.


00:31:38.680 --> 00:31:41.274
<i>The whole stadium</i>


00:31:42.840 --> 00:31:45.638
<i>is an ovation</i>


00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:50.749
<i>we're the red and blue</i>


00:31:51.840 --> 00:31:55.628
<i>it doesn't matter</i>
<i>where we come from,</i>


00:31:56.400 --> 00:32:00.109
<i>be it South or North</i>


00:32:01.160 --> 00:32:04.675
<i>we all agree, now,</i>
<i>we all agree</i>


00:32:05.800 --> 00:32:09.679
<i>a flag makes us</i>
<i>brothers and sisters</i>


00:32:10.240 --> 00:32:11.309
<i>Barça!</i>


00:32:11.640 --> 00:32:12.834
<i>Barça!</i>


00:32:13.800 --> 00:32:15.950
<i>Barça!</i>


00:32:17.280 --> 00:32:19.669
Why don't you change channels?


00:32:21.160 --> 00:32:22.229
What would you like to watch?


00:32:22.400 --> 00:32:24.595
I can't stay, I have stuff to do.


00:32:24.760 --> 00:32:26.034
Stay a bit longer.


00:32:26.200 --> 00:32:27.110
It's late.


00:32:27.280 --> 00:32:28.269
Just a little while.


00:32:29.320 --> 00:32:30.719
Wouldn't you rather sleep?


00:32:30.880 --> 00:32:32.199
I'm not tired.


00:32:32.360 --> 00:32:33.793
I haven't had dinner yet.


00:32:34.920 --> 00:32:37.115
Please, stay.


00:32:37.680 --> 00:32:38.829
Just for a minute.


00:32:39.360 --> 00:32:40.588
Ok.


00:32:42.000 --> 00:32:43.399
I'll stay for a minute.


00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:45.589
Take a seat.


00:32:46.240 --> 00:32:48.435
My husband is very late.


00:32:49.520 --> 00:32:51.112
Are you scared he won't come back?


00:32:51.280 --> 00:32:52.952
Why shouldn't he?


00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:54.548
I don't know.


00:32:56.560 --> 00:32:59.950
Do you know I met my husband
at the Opera?


00:33:00.680 --> 00:33:04.309
It was raining and my cousin and I
were waiting for a cab.


00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:06.471
He saw we were so bored


00:33:07.120 --> 00:33:09.588
he told us how he had met Callas.


00:33:09.760 --> 00:33:13.639
She'd lost a puppy on the Rambles
and he'd found it.


00:33:14.120 --> 00:33:17.192
Your husband asked me to show him
how to load the gun.


00:33:18.240 --> 00:33:20.356
- You put the bullets in here?
- I don't have any.


00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:23.114
Let me, let me.


00:33:24.360 --> 00:33:27.670
He's more scared of guns than me.
I'm used to them.


00:33:27.840 --> 00:33:29.592
Have you ever shot a gun?


00:33:30.880 --> 00:33:32.472
Not really.


00:33:33.600 --> 00:33:35.556
My grandfather had one.


00:33:35.720 --> 00:33:37.950
He bought it for the Tragic Week.


00:33:38.120 --> 00:33:42.079
He was afraid his employees
would lynch him.


00:33:42.760 --> 00:33:44.751
The gun ended up in a closet


00:33:44.920 --> 00:33:47.309
and my cousins and I played with it.


00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:50.638
- Do you know how to load it?
- No, and I don't want to.


00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:55.991
Nobody wants a gun close by,


00:33:56.160 --> 00:33:59.470
but everybody wants
their money protected.


00:34:00.600 --> 00:34:04.593
Between the van and the safe,
not even one note can be missed.


00:34:05.240 --> 00:34:07.071
I didn't know you did banks too.


00:34:07.480 --> 00:34:11.439
You can stand a truncheon at home,
but a gun is too much.


00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:13.397
Your husband isn't such an hypocrite.


00:34:13.560 --> 00:34:16.028
My husband's ill.


00:34:16.640 --> 00:34:18.073
You'd better leave him alone.


00:34:19.040 --> 00:34:23.033
When I rented the room,
I thought you wanted a guard


00:34:23.600 --> 00:34:25.989
so you wouldn't be scared at night.


00:34:26.440 --> 00:34:28.908
You're never home, now.


00:34:29.360 --> 00:34:32.352
My bosses think I live with my mum.


00:34:33.200 --> 00:34:35.589
They don't like guards
who live alone,


00:34:35.760 --> 00:34:37.751
or have marital problems.


00:34:37.920 --> 00:34:40.036
They think you live with your mum?


00:34:41.520 --> 00:34:45.229
At the beginning you treated me
as if I was your child.


00:34:47.200 --> 00:34:50.988
You were willing to come see me play
on Sunday morning.


00:34:51.400 --> 00:34:53.356
It's good you didn't come.


00:34:53.760 --> 00:34:56.991
Until you came, I didn't know anyone
who liked football,


00:34:57.160 --> 00:34:58.957
not even my dad.


00:34:59.760 --> 00:35:03.753
He said he went to the game,
but he went to a whorehouse.


00:35:04.400 --> 00:35:06.470
We all knew, at home.


00:35:06.840 --> 00:35:08.831
Going to the game meant whores.


00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.116
Maybe your husband went
to one today.


00:35:15.120 --> 00:35:16.553
Did I hurt you?


00:35:36.680 --> 00:35:39.148
I can't be your mother.


00:35:40.160 --> 00:35:42.230
I've already had a daughter.


00:35:42.680 --> 00:35:43.874
Where is she?


00:35:45.400 --> 00:35:47.675
She died in the most stupid way.


00:35:52.720 --> 00:35:56.508
She was run over by a bus
on Passeig de Gràcia long ago.


00:35:56.680 --> 00:35:59.148
0ne of those which went
in the wrong direction,


00:35:59.320 --> 00:36:01.276
they killed a lot of people.


00:36:02.840 --> 00:36:05.638
Ramon almost went crazy.


00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:08.956
Was this her room?


00:36:11.240 --> 00:36:12.958
My daughter's?


00:36:15.600 --> 00:36:16.589
Yes.


00:36:20.240 --> 00:36:22.834
- You'd better go to sleep, now.
- I can't.


00:36:23.360 --> 00:36:25.999
- Does your knee hurt?
- I've got insomnia.


00:36:26.160 --> 00:36:28.469
Would you like a tablet?
Ramon has many.


00:36:28.640 --> 00:36:32.235
Don't leave yet.
Stay until I fall asleep.


00:36:33.200 --> 00:36:35.919
I'll stay
until you close your eyes.


00:36:37.160 --> 00:36:38.309
Lie down.


00:36:44.080 --> 00:36:45.672
No, don't turn it off.


00:36:46.720 --> 00:36:49.439
- Do you sleep with the TV on?
- Yes.


00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:58.628
You know what's worst
about working nights?


00:36:59.160 --> 00:36:59.797
What?


00:37:00.320 --> 00:37:02.515
The last hour before finishing.


00:37:07.520 --> 00:37:11.229
It's the longest, and when
you hear the strangest noises.


00:37:14.880 --> 00:37:17.997
The rest of the night
the noises are normal,


00:37:23.560 --> 00:37:27.519
but then you hear things
you haven't heard before,


00:37:32.320 --> 00:37:34.914
as if your hearing
could pick out everything.


00:37:35.360 --> 00:37:37.078
Even people.


00:37:41.040 --> 00:37:43.235
Voices of people who are not there.


00:37:45.520 --> 00:37:49.479
I sometimes hear voices too,
but I don't listen to them.


00:37:49.800 --> 00:37:51.995
When I hear them,
I start singing.


00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:53.036
Singing?


00:37:53.840 --> 00:37:54.989
Close your eyes.


00:37:55.360 --> 00:37:56.156
I can't.


00:37:56.600 --> 00:37:58.033
Of course you can.


00:37:58.840 --> 00:38:00.239
Don't leave yet.


00:38:00.400 --> 00:38:01.435
I'm not leaving.


00:38:04.880 --> 00:38:07.030
<i>Sono andati?</i>


00:38:07.880 --> 00:38:10.440
<i>Fingevo di dormire</i>


00:38:11.800 --> 00:38:15.793
<i>perché volli con te sola restare.</i>


00:38:18.120 --> 00:38:21.237
<i>Ho tante cose</i>


00:38:21.400 --> 00:38:24.153
<i>che ti voglio dire,</i>


00:38:25.640 --> 00:38:29.599
<i>o una sola,</i>
<i>ma grande come il mare,</i>


00:38:30.240 --> 00:38:34.119
<i>come il mare</i>
<i>profonda ed infinita...</i>


00:38:35.160 --> 00:38:37.879
<i>Sei il mio amore</i>


00:38:39.040 --> 00:38:42.828
<i>e tutta la mia vita.</i>


00:40:23.520 --> 00:40:24.509
Are you alright?


00:40:25.880 --> 00:40:27.279
Yes, excuse me.


00:40:27.720 --> 00:40:29.312
I fell asleep.


00:40:29.480 --> 00:40:32.631
- No, no, don't get up.
- Sit down.


00:40:32.800 --> 00:40:35.598
- You must be very tired.
- Thanks.


00:40:42.560 --> 00:40:44.710
It's ok, leave them there.


00:40:48.920 --> 00:40:51.275
Shouldn't you stop working now?


00:40:51.440 --> 00:40:53.237
I'm working while I can.


00:40:53.400 --> 00:40:55.470
I'm very slow now,
like a tortoise.


00:40:56.280 --> 00:40:57.679
What happened?


00:40:59.080 --> 00:41:00.195
Fuck!


00:41:00.360 --> 00:41:04.069
They sharpened the knifes
and I cut myself, but it's nothing.


00:41:06.560 --> 00:41:08.471
Were you waiting for me?


00:41:09.520 --> 00:41:11.875
Yes, but I fell asleep,


00:41:12.040 --> 00:41:13.359
I'm sorry.


00:41:16.040 --> 00:41:17.678
Nice slippers.


00:41:20.920 --> 00:41:23.514
Do you like them? They were a gift.


00:41:26.160 --> 00:41:29.277
This too.
The best Spanish invention.


00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:32.277
Too bad I can't use it at work.


00:41:32.440 --> 00:41:35.637
We have a fan which only
messes up our hair.


00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:37.991
Summer here is unbearable.


00:41:38.600 --> 00:41:39.828
Really?


00:41:40.760 --> 00:41:43.638
Do you need any help on Monday?


00:41:43.800 --> 00:41:44.755
Monday?


00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:46.639
To move out.


00:41:49.360 --> 00:41:52.955
No, it's ok.
Some friends said they'd come.


00:41:53.120 --> 00:41:55.680
The same ones
who didn't come last time?


00:41:56.240 --> 00:41:57.639
They're doing me a favour.


00:41:58.000 --> 00:41:59.638
It's hard at the wholesale market.


00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:02.196
They load trucks all night.


00:42:02.440 --> 00:42:04.192
So much food is wasted here.


00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:06.317
It makes me sick.


00:42:07.480 --> 00:42:09.710
Why don't they ever collide?


00:42:11.320 --> 00:42:13.038
The fishbowl is so small.


00:42:15.160 --> 00:42:18.311
As I can't tell them apart,
I didn't name them.


00:42:19.920 --> 00:42:22.957
If your friends
can't come on Monday,


00:42:23.560 --> 00:42:26.358
I can find someone else
to help you.


00:42:28.120 --> 00:42:31.078
I didn't know you rented this place.


00:42:31.240 --> 00:42:32.116
Didn't you?


00:42:32.280 --> 00:42:34.635
No, your wife told me.


00:42:35.320 --> 00:42:38.835
Yes, we always have.


00:42:39.320 --> 00:42:41.788
I never talked to your wife much.


00:42:42.560 --> 00:42:44.869
I realised lately
that when pregnant


00:42:45.040 --> 00:42:47.110
people open their hearts to you.


00:42:48.480 --> 00:42:50.277
What else did she say?


00:42:50.840 --> 00:42:53.479
She asked if I'd come
to visit you.


00:42:54.240 --> 00:42:55.275
Really?


00:42:55.800 --> 00:42:58.109
But I'm not sure she meant it.


00:42:58.440 --> 00:43:00.431
I said I'd call before coming.


00:43:01.120 --> 00:43:04.112
She also asked if I had friends
in the neighbourhood.


00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:07.953
We used to know all the neighbours,
but now


00:43:08.120 --> 00:43:10.714
we don't even know
who lives next door.


00:43:10.880 --> 00:43:13.269
So your wife said.


00:43:14.160 --> 00:43:17.869
Now that I'll have more time,
I'm going to learn Catalan.


00:43:18.040 --> 00:43:21.191
You can speak to me in Catalan,
so I can get used to it.


00:43:22.440 --> 00:43:24.715
But you won't understand.


00:43:24.880 --> 00:43:27.348
I understand everything
at the restaurant,


00:43:28.000 --> 00:43:30.912
though I hardly leave the kitchen.


00:43:32.080 --> 00:43:36.039
You know, the funniest word,
for me, is <i>escamarlà.</i>


00:43:36.200 --> 00:43:36.871
<i>Escamarlà.</i>


00:43:40.360 --> 00:43:42.590
Yes, <i>escamarlà.</i>


00:43:49.280 --> 00:43:52.078
Are you going to keep working
at the restaurant?


00:43:53.320 --> 00:43:55.515
Where else could I work?


00:43:56.800 --> 00:43:58.279
Nobody's offered better.


00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:07.833
A few days ago, a woman stopped me
in the street


00:44:08.000 --> 00:44:10.434
to ask whether I wanted
to work for her.


00:44:10.600 --> 00:44:13.751
I thought it was strange,
because I'll be useless soon.


00:44:13.920 --> 00:44:16.115
So, casually, I asked some questions.


00:44:16.280 --> 00:44:17.713
You know what she wanted?


00:44:26.400 --> 00:44:28.516
She wanted my baby when I had it.


00:44:28.680 --> 00:44:32.389
She didn't put it that way,
but I could see what she meant.


00:44:32.880 --> 00:44:35.633
You must be careful now
with the baby.


00:44:36.240 --> 00:44:38.117
You can't get distracted.


00:44:38.280 --> 00:44:41.238
Especially when crossing
the street,


00:44:41.400 --> 00:44:43.436
always check both ways.


00:44:44.840 --> 00:44:48.150
You said exactly the same thing
when I moved in.


00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:49.476
Really?


00:44:49.640 --> 00:44:53.428
I thought you wanted to distract
me from the size of the room.


00:44:53.920 --> 00:44:56.434
I didn't think you'd stay so long.


00:44:56.680 --> 00:44:58.272
Neither did I.


00:44:58.840 --> 00:45:02.037
But it stuck to me like a shell.


00:45:04.400 --> 00:45:06.516
If you're staying,
you'd better sit.


00:45:14.040 --> 00:45:15.837
At least the bed is comfy.


00:45:17.560 --> 00:45:18.629
Yes.


00:45:21.120 --> 00:45:23.111
Look into my eyes.


00:45:24.360 --> 00:45:27.909
- Don't do the same as everyone else.
- Who?


00:45:28.080 --> 00:45:31.390
Here, for someone to look you
in the eye, you have to fall down.


00:45:31.760 --> 00:45:33.193
Did you fall?


00:45:33.360 --> 00:45:35.828
No, but sometimes
I feel like falling,


00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:39.231
just so they'll help me to stand
and ask if I'm ok.


00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:44.552
You have to be careful now
with the baby.


00:45:45.240 --> 00:45:46.639
You've already said that.


00:45:48.720 --> 00:45:50.438
What would you name the baby?


00:45:52.760 --> 00:45:53.715
I don't know.


00:45:54.200 --> 00:45:56.350
What if I named it


00:45:57.920 --> 00:45:59.319
<i>escamarlà</i>?


00:46:01.440 --> 00:46:02.634
Just kidding.


00:46:04.600 --> 00:46:05.635
Of course.


00:46:06.200 --> 00:46:08.031
I also asked your wife.


00:46:08.440 --> 00:46:10.829
- What did she say?
- She didn't know.


00:46:11.640 --> 00:46:16.031
When you don't want to answer,
you say you don't know or <i>viceversa.</i>


00:46:16.600 --> 00:46:17.953
If you like,


00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:21.798
I'll think of a name and tell you.


00:46:21.960 --> 00:46:25.032
- You won't.
- lf I think of one, I will.


00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:31.388
You never asked about the father.


00:46:34.280 --> 00:46:37.431
I thought you would tell us
if you wanted to.


00:46:39.520 --> 00:46:42.239
And if I said it was yours?


00:46:43.240 --> 00:46:43.831
Mine?


00:46:44.360 --> 00:46:45.952
You must have thought about it.


00:46:57.440 --> 00:46:59.237
It was only once,


00:47:00.480 --> 00:47:01.674
and I'm sick...


00:47:06.720 --> 00:47:09.712
If it wasn't for you, I don't know
what I'd have done.


00:47:10.600 --> 00:47:12.795
I was very sad, too.


00:47:13.080 --> 00:47:16.789
I'd been sacked without pay.


00:47:17.080 --> 00:47:19.071
You didn't tell me.


00:47:20.520 --> 00:47:24.513
I thought you did it
because you felt sorry for me.


00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:26.592
That, too.


00:47:26.840 --> 00:47:28.558
I won't kid you.


00:47:29.240 --> 00:47:31.470
I thought of having an abortion,


00:47:31.640 --> 00:47:35.269
all my friends said
I should have one,


00:47:36.800 --> 00:47:40.315
because you're old


00:47:40.920 --> 00:47:43.115
and the baby could have problems.


00:47:43.280 --> 00:47:45.157
But I decided to have it,


00:47:45.760 --> 00:47:47.955
with the baby
I wouldn't feel so alone.


00:47:51.760 --> 00:47:53.432
Did you tell my wife?


00:47:53.600 --> 00:47:56.876
What? That it's yours? What for?


00:47:57.840 --> 00:47:58.829
I don't know.


00:48:00.280 --> 00:48:03.670
- Has your wife ever eaten anyone?
- Sorry?


00:48:03.840 --> 00:48:07.071
- Have you ever seen her eat anyone?
- No.


00:48:07.240 --> 00:48:08.992
Why are you so scared of her?


00:48:09.160 --> 00:48:11.037
I'm not scared of her.


00:48:11.200 --> 00:48:14.556
I just don't want
to make her worry more.


00:48:15.840 --> 00:48:18.718
She is really worried about you.


00:48:24.760 --> 00:48:26.352
I'll leave the bowl for you.


00:48:27.160 --> 00:48:29.390
No, take it, it's yours.


00:48:29.880 --> 00:48:32.519
Don't feed them too much,
or they'll die.


00:48:35.280 --> 00:48:38.113
Have you thought of which hospital
you'll go to?


00:48:39.280 --> 00:48:40.599
Why do you ask?


00:48:41.120 --> 00:48:41.916
Just because.


00:48:42.080 --> 00:48:44.514
You were never interested before.


00:48:45.040 --> 00:48:47.554
When you get here,
I'm usually in bed.


00:48:47.880 --> 00:48:49.598
You waited for me today, though,


00:48:49.760 --> 00:48:53.753
just to tell me to hurry up
and pack my stuff.


00:49:00.400 --> 00:49:02.197
I guess your wife sent you.


00:49:02.720 --> 00:49:03.516
No.


00:49:05.160 --> 00:49:08.516
Well, yes,
because she had to go out


00:49:09.640 --> 00:49:11.312
and I wanted to know you're fine.


00:49:12.040 --> 00:49:13.837
You can see I am.


00:49:15.120 --> 00:49:16.109
Yes.


00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:17.994
Are you fine?


00:49:18.240 --> 00:49:21.835
I get tired quicker than before,
but I'm fine.


00:49:23.480 --> 00:49:26.995
- Does it hurt a lot?
- No, not a lot.


00:49:27.760 --> 00:49:31.036
I'm scared it will hurt
when the baby is born.


00:49:31.200 --> 00:49:34.272
I have never felt real pain,
not even a toothache.


00:49:34.520 --> 00:49:36.511
I don't know if I'll stand it.


00:49:37.040 --> 00:49:38.109
Of course you will.


00:49:38.560 --> 00:49:39.709
Maybe not.


00:49:41.000 --> 00:49:42.479
During the war,


00:49:42.760 --> 00:49:45.433
I thought I wouldn't stand it,
but I did.


00:49:45.600 --> 00:49:49.434
I told you not to talk
about the war or dead people.


00:49:49.600 --> 00:49:51.795
I was just going to talk about...


00:49:51.960 --> 00:49:54.952
At home everybody talked
about dead people.


00:49:55.120 --> 00:49:57.509
All day, all night.


00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:00.958
There's nothing worse than
the smell of a wake.


00:50:01.120 --> 00:50:02.519
That's true.


00:50:03.880 --> 00:50:07.475
When you're a kid,
you can run out and play,


00:50:07.760 --> 00:50:09.955
but when you grow up,
you have to go farther away.


00:50:10.960 --> 00:50:13.315
Nobody should be made to go
to a wake.


00:50:13.480 --> 00:50:16.472
Did I say I was forced to?
Did I?


00:50:17.400 --> 00:50:21.393
Waiting on hours of traffic,
that's what I'm forced to.


00:50:22.400 --> 00:50:24.960
Working in a kitchen
being hot all day,


00:50:25.120 --> 00:50:26.872
that too is an obligation.


00:50:28.440 --> 00:50:29.111
That's true.


00:50:29.280 --> 00:50:32.272
Don't just say I'm right,
like you do with your wife.


00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:34.954
I'd rather you argued.
Why don't you argue?


00:50:35.480 --> 00:50:37.630
There's nothing to argue about.


00:50:37.800 --> 00:50:39.358
Then shut up.


00:50:40.960 --> 00:50:43.554
I'm sorry, I didn't mean that.


00:50:43.920 --> 00:50:47.310
But sometimes it's better to argue
than to say yes to everything.


00:50:48.600 --> 00:50:49.589
That's true.


00:50:50.080 --> 00:50:51.877
You're hopeless.


00:50:55.600 --> 00:50:56.589
Should I leave?


00:50:58.760 --> 00:51:00.159
Your wife


00:51:01.320 --> 00:51:04.790
asked for my new address,
but I didn't give it to her.


00:51:07.240 --> 00:51:08.229
Well.


00:51:08.720 --> 00:51:12.030
When you start asking,
you want to know more and more


00:51:12.800 --> 00:51:14.597
until it's a complete mess.


00:51:15.160 --> 00:51:16.036
Yes.


00:51:18.280 --> 00:51:19.269
You know?


00:51:20.880 --> 00:51:22.438
Where I come from,


00:51:22.600 --> 00:51:25.558
women who ask and tell the truth


00:51:25.720 --> 00:51:27.711
remain alone for life.


00:51:29.680 --> 00:51:32.240
I've never told the truth


00:51:34.240 --> 00:51:35.639
and I've never been alone.


00:51:35.800 --> 00:51:37.791
It's not the same with men.


00:51:37.960 --> 00:51:40.394
Men always have
some woman or other.


00:51:42.120 --> 00:51:43.838
Do you always tell the truth?


00:51:46.040 --> 00:51:47.837
I was never so brave.


00:51:50.040 --> 00:51:51.837
Let's do something.


00:51:53.600 --> 00:51:56.319
I'll ask something
and you ask something back.


00:51:56.840 --> 00:51:57.875
What for?


00:51:58.360 --> 00:51:59.873
To tell the truth.


00:52:01.240 --> 00:52:02.639
All the truth?


00:52:04.120 --> 00:52:04.916
Yes.


00:52:07.040 --> 00:52:08.234
What do you want to ask?


00:52:08.400 --> 00:52:10.789
No, you first.


00:52:10.960 --> 00:52:13.599
No, I'd rather you went first.


00:52:15.640 --> 00:52:16.516
All right.


00:52:20.520 --> 00:52:23.751
Why didn't you tell me
the baby was mine before?


00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:29.352
You waited for me tonight.


00:52:30.520 --> 00:52:34.308
If you had waited before,
I would have told you then.


00:52:36.640 --> 00:52:37.868
That's why?


00:52:38.040 --> 00:52:40.508
I never thought
of asking for money.


00:52:41.440 --> 00:52:43.510
If not, I would've told your wife.


00:52:45.960 --> 00:52:48.793
- Can I ask now?
- Yes.


00:52:49.960 --> 00:52:51.518
No, it's embarrassing.


00:52:51.680 --> 00:52:53.193
Go ahead and ask.


00:52:55.480 --> 00:52:57.357
Why do you dress up as a woman?


00:52:59.840 --> 00:53:03.116
You left your door open
and I almost went in.


00:53:17.480 --> 00:53:19.630
When I worked at the Opera


00:53:19.960 --> 00:53:23.157
I sometimes dressed up
in opera costumes,


00:53:24.200 --> 00:53:27.590
and I still do that sometimes.


00:53:28.200 --> 00:53:29.189
As a woman?


00:53:30.040 --> 00:53:34.033
When you dress up,
it's like being someone else.


00:53:35.840 --> 00:53:39.196
As if the costume
gave you something


00:53:39.800 --> 00:53:41.597
you are not.


00:53:43.640 --> 00:53:45.232
Do you understand?


00:53:45.640 --> 00:53:48.837
Yes, I sometimes dressed up
in carnivals.


00:53:49.000 --> 00:53:50.479
No, no, no.


00:53:51.240 --> 00:53:53.435
I do it at home, just for me.


00:53:56.360 --> 00:53:57.918
The dress wasn't very nice.


00:53:59.760 --> 00:54:00.556
I know.


00:54:01.480 --> 00:54:03.550
I could help you
find another one.


00:54:03.880 --> 00:54:05.279
No, it's not necessary.


00:54:05.440 --> 00:54:08.034
- Did you choose that one?
- Yes.


00:54:08.920 --> 00:54:12.356
Didn't they ask
who it was for at the shop?


00:54:13.480 --> 00:54:14.276
No.


00:54:14.640 --> 00:54:18.599
I would have asked. You see?
That's why I'm alone.


00:54:18.960 --> 00:54:20.632
Will you tell someone?


00:54:20.800 --> 00:54:23.872
- Does your wife know?
- Yes.


00:54:24.040 --> 00:54:25.393
What did she say?


00:54:27.520 --> 00:54:28.236
Nothing.


00:54:29.720 --> 00:54:30.994
Wait.


00:54:35.480 --> 00:54:36.515
Lie down.


00:54:37.120 --> 00:54:38.109
What for?


00:54:38.640 --> 00:54:40.756
It's not enough just to dress up.


00:54:41.440 --> 00:54:42.589
What do you mean?


00:54:42.760 --> 00:54:44.159
Lie down.


00:54:54.360 --> 00:54:55.236
No.


00:54:56.880 --> 00:54:58.313
Don't move.


00:55:00.640 --> 00:55:02.312
Have you ever tried it?


00:55:03.400 --> 00:55:04.037
No.


00:55:04.520 --> 00:55:06.511
You wash your face
before bed, don't you?


00:55:06.760 --> 00:55:09.752
Yes, but it's very late.


00:55:10.080 --> 00:55:11.957
It'll only take a second.


00:57:13.680 --> 00:57:15.636
- Did I scare you?
- No.


00:57:15.920 --> 00:57:17.512
Who opened the door?


00:57:17.800 --> 00:57:20.519
Someone was going out
and I went in.


00:57:24.960 --> 00:57:27.758
- I'll give you a key.
- It's not necessary.


00:57:32.360 --> 00:57:34.920
What are they doing upstairs?


00:57:35.080 --> 00:57:36.593
Wasn't that an earthquake?


00:57:36.760 --> 00:57:40.036
There are no earthquakes in Barcelona.
There never have been.


00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:49.712
You look tired.


00:57:50.120 --> 00:57:50.996
No.


00:57:51.480 --> 00:57:52.595
Have you had dinner?


00:57:53.560 --> 00:57:54.629
At the hospital.


00:57:54.800 --> 00:57:58.236
In front of 4 anorexic girls
I'm teaching how to eat.


00:58:06.560 --> 00:58:09.916
Anorexia overwhelms me
and fascinates me.


00:58:10.720 --> 00:58:11.948
Fascinates you?


00:58:13.040 --> 00:58:15.713
- Do you remember today's lunch?
- Yes.


00:58:16.480 --> 00:58:19.358
And yesterday's?
And the day before's?


00:58:21.360 --> 00:58:24.033
They remember every crumb
we make them swallow.


00:58:24.520 --> 00:58:26.590
One of them said today


00:58:26.760 --> 00:58:29.354
that people look at her
as if she were a pig


00:58:29.520 --> 00:58:32.318
being fed to be slaughtered.


00:58:32.840 --> 00:58:34.068
She might be right.


00:58:34.480 --> 00:58:35.708
Might she?


00:58:37.800 --> 00:58:39.518
You know why I became a surgeon?


00:58:40.120 --> 00:58:41.917
To look for the soul.


00:58:42.720 --> 00:58:44.517
I never found it.
It wasn't there.


00:58:45.080 --> 00:58:47.435
You thought you'd find it
operating?


00:58:47.720 --> 00:58:50.712
There are extraordinary things
in the human body.


00:58:50.880 --> 00:58:53.155
Why couldn't the soul be there?


00:58:53.640 --> 00:58:56.359
Why couldn't it be tangible


00:58:57.040 --> 00:58:59.315
like kidneys or intestines?


00:59:00.600 --> 00:59:03.751
Religion and psychiatry
haven't been able to show the soul.


00:59:08.120 --> 00:59:12.113
And they've had time enough,
especially religion.


00:59:18.520 --> 00:59:20.431
I went to a bullfight today.


00:59:20.600 --> 00:59:22.556
Most of the audience
were foreigners.


00:59:22.720 --> 00:59:25.598
After the second bull,
they supported the bulls


00:59:25.760 --> 00:59:27.273
instead of the bullfighters.


00:59:29.080 --> 00:59:29.990
And you?


00:59:30.200 --> 00:59:32.509
I left before it was over.


00:59:33.160 --> 00:59:36.152
Then I walked to the old train station.


00:59:37.240 --> 00:59:41.233
Remember, I took you there
as a kid


00:59:41.880 --> 00:59:44.314
to see the trains come and go?


00:59:52.160 --> 00:59:53.878
Yes, I do remember.


00:59:56.040 --> 00:59:59.112
When did you last catch a train?


00:59:59.360 --> 01:00:00.759
A long time ago.


01:00:01.120 --> 01:00:02.109
Where did you go?


01:00:03.160 --> 01:00:04.115
To Venice.


01:00:04.760 --> 01:00:06.478
Venice?


01:00:06.800 --> 01:00:09.109
First to Milan, then Venice.


01:00:09.800 --> 01:00:12.314
That's where I first saw colours.


01:00:12.760 --> 01:00:13.829
Which colours?


01:00:14.480 --> 01:00:15.674
All of them.


01:00:16.760 --> 01:00:18.432
What colours can you see now?


01:00:18.960 --> 01:00:20.279
Black and white.


01:00:20.960 --> 01:00:22.029
Just that?


01:00:24.400 --> 01:00:27.392
The last time I saw them
was during the Olympic Games.


01:00:27.560 --> 01:00:30.358
I was a volunteer.
Everybody was euphoric,


01:00:30.520 --> 01:00:33.512
athletes parading
and the audience applauding.


01:00:34.080 --> 01:00:37.117
Then I took my trousers off.


01:00:37.280 --> 01:00:39.714
- You did?
- Yes.


01:00:41.120 --> 01:00:43.350
I can never tell when you'rejoking.


01:00:43.920 --> 01:00:45.911
I'm always serious.


01:00:47.280 --> 01:00:50.477
I never understood
why you volunteered.


01:00:52.800 --> 01:00:55.075
They needed doctors,
and the psychiatrist told me


01:00:55.240 --> 01:00:57.515
It'd help me come out of myself.


01:00:58.640 --> 01:01:01.359
- Do you still go?
- Not anymore.


01:01:03.840 --> 01:01:07.310
Endogamy is incurable, sister.


01:01:07.480 --> 01:01:10.677
You can tell by looking
at the upper class families left.


01:01:13.560 --> 01:01:14.788
Why did you call?


01:01:17.040 --> 01:01:19.952
I hadn't heard from you
in a long time.


01:01:22.360 --> 01:01:25.193
Do you remember the last time
we talked?


01:01:26.080 --> 01:01:26.990
No.


01:01:27.520 --> 01:01:30.318
Ramon is really ill. Did you know?


01:01:30.720 --> 01:01:31.709
You told me.


01:01:37.600 --> 01:01:39.113
Do you know who's singing?


01:01:39.520 --> 01:01:40.316
No.


01:01:42.600 --> 01:01:44.079
Callas.


01:01:45.120 --> 01:01:47.270
I never got you to like opera,


01:01:47.440 --> 01:01:49.590
or to go to there with me.


01:01:51.760 --> 01:01:52.590
Do you still go?


01:01:52.920 --> 01:01:54.876
Not anymore.


01:01:55.840 --> 01:01:57.717
It's expensive, and going alone...


01:01:57.880 --> 01:02:00.075
If you like we can go.
I'll pay.


01:02:01.040 --> 01:02:02.712
Would you go with me?


01:02:03.200 --> 01:02:05.191
- On one condition.
- What?


01:02:05.600 --> 01:02:09.354
- Afterwards, we set it on fire.
- The Opera House?


01:02:09.960 --> 01:02:13.714
They'd build another one.
We should burn something else.


01:02:14.440 --> 01:02:16.635
The Agbar Tower, for instance.


01:02:16.920 --> 01:02:20.469
And we wouldn't leave it at that,
then we'd burn...


01:02:21.160 --> 01:02:22.354
the MACBA.


01:02:22.640 --> 01:02:24.073
And then?


01:02:24.360 --> 01:02:25.395
If they don't stop us,


01:02:25.560 --> 01:02:28.791
there are some skyscrapers
which would burn wonderfully.


01:02:28.960 --> 01:02:30.632
Don't forget the National Theatre.


01:02:30.800 --> 01:02:31.835
And the Sagrada Família.


01:02:32.000 --> 01:02:34.468
It's not finished,
but we could burn it.


01:02:34.720 --> 01:02:36.517
And Catalunya Square.


01:02:36.920 --> 01:02:39.115
And Passeig de Gràcia.


01:02:43.960 --> 01:02:47.350
Once it was burnt down,
I'd plant a vineyard,


01:02:47.520 --> 01:02:50.512
as a homage to phylloxera,
which made it possible.


01:02:53.400 --> 01:02:55.277
Why did you call?


01:02:58.040 --> 01:03:00.110
I wanted you know how you're doing.


01:03:01.480 --> 01:03:02.959
That's all?


01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:07.034
We've kicked out the tenants.
They're all leaving next week.


01:03:08.560 --> 01:03:10.869
You wanted to tell me that?


01:03:11.720 --> 01:03:14.712
We thought it would be best
to be alone.


01:03:15.560 --> 01:03:16.879
What for?


01:03:17.320 --> 01:03:19.197
Ramon wants to die at home.


01:03:19.800 --> 01:03:21.950
- Is he sure?
- Yes.


01:03:22.480 --> 01:03:26.189
- It'll be difficult for the both of you.
- We know.


01:03:26.360 --> 01:03:28.715
If you're really sure,
it's fine by me.


01:03:31.600 --> 01:03:33.670
Will you come if I call you?


01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:35.788
Why?


01:03:36.800 --> 01:03:39.678
He said he wants
to ask you something.


01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:41.194
- Me?
- Yes.


01:03:41.920 --> 01:03:43.717
Why doesn't he ask his doctor?


01:03:44.600 --> 01:03:47.194
- He wants to talk to you.
- I'm not an oncologist.


01:03:47.360 --> 01:03:49.874
It's nothing to do
with the illness.


01:03:50.040 --> 01:03:51.109
What is it?


01:03:51.840 --> 01:03:54.673
He didn't want to tell me.
It must be a man thing.


01:03:55.440 --> 01:03:56.236
Man thing?


01:03:57.240 --> 01:04:00.152
He must be embarrassed to tell me.


01:04:00.560 --> 01:04:03.916
Lately he's just talked about the war,
the day it ended.


01:04:04.080 --> 01:04:05.593
He'd better talk to his doctor.


01:04:09.160 --> 01:04:11.310
You won't come, then?


01:04:13.720 --> 01:04:14.596
I don't know.


01:04:17.680 --> 01:04:18.669
If you come,


01:04:20.600 --> 01:04:22.875
I'll let you read my diary.


01:04:27.000 --> 01:04:29.673
- You still keep one?
- Yes, I do.


01:04:33.760 --> 01:04:36.194
- Everyday?
- Almost.


01:04:41.040 --> 01:04:43.634
Can I read it from the start?


01:04:44.600 --> 01:04:45.589
Yes.


01:04:49.280 --> 01:04:50.269
Yes.


01:04:51.280 --> 01:04:53.748
- Will you come?
- Show it to me now.


01:04:53.920 --> 01:04:57.117
- No. Next time you come.
- I want to read it now.


01:04:59.720 --> 01:05:03.713
I'll give it to you
if you read it after you leave.


01:05:03.960 --> 01:05:05.678
Can I take it with me?


01:05:06.680 --> 01:05:07.590
Yes.


01:05:07.760 --> 01:05:09.079
Where is it?


01:05:11.600 --> 01:05:13.033
In that drawer.


01:05:17.520 --> 01:05:20.478
I've always been scared
of people who lock things.


01:05:20.640 --> 01:05:23.837
It's the only locked drawer
in the house.


01:05:32.920 --> 01:05:36.151
Father locked everything.
Do you remember?


01:05:40.800 --> 01:05:42.313
The green is the oldest.


01:05:45.760 --> 01:05:46.636
This one?


01:05:48.360 --> 01:05:49.349
Yes.


01:05:52.960 --> 01:05:56.077
"Dad came to my room tonight..."


01:05:56.240 --> 01:05:59.232
- Has anyone else read it?
- No.


01:06:00.120 --> 01:06:01.951
- Not even your husband?
- No.


01:06:02.120 --> 01:06:03.872
I'd never seen your writing.


01:06:04.200 --> 01:06:06.794
I told you not to read it here.


01:06:17.160 --> 01:06:19.151
Don't you go to the hairdresser's?


01:06:19.480 --> 01:06:21.198
I don't get out much.


01:06:21.360 --> 01:06:22.475
Why?


01:06:22.640 --> 01:06:25.518
I even have food delivered.


01:06:26.200 --> 01:06:28.509
- Do you have enough money?
- Yes.


01:06:29.320 --> 01:06:31.470
And when he dies?


01:06:32.320 --> 01:06:33.469
What?


01:06:34.400 --> 01:06:36.630
You'll only have half of his pension.


01:06:36.800 --> 01:06:38.597
I'll get by.


01:06:40.360 --> 01:06:43.352
- Will you look for new tenants?
- I don't know.


01:06:44.960 --> 01:06:47.235
If you need any money, let me know.


01:06:47.400 --> 01:06:49.789
You're always broke.


01:06:50.600 --> 01:06:53.478
I wish we were rich, like before.


01:06:54.680 --> 01:06:55.669
Yes.


01:07:04.520 --> 01:07:07.990
Can I comb your hair,
like I did as a child?


01:07:08.560 --> 01:07:10.790
Your hair was long and I combed it.


01:07:10.960 --> 01:07:12.552
I thought I'd have it cut.


01:07:12.720 --> 01:07:15.314
No, don't. I won't let you.


01:07:15.800 --> 01:07:18.109
- Where's the comb?
- In the bathroom.


01:07:18.280 --> 01:07:19.918
- Go get it.
- No.


01:07:20.280 --> 01:07:23.556
- Then I'll come again and take you.
- Where?


01:07:23.760 --> 01:07:25.079
To the hairdresser's.


01:07:25.240 --> 01:07:27.549
We could go to the hairdresser's
and then the Opera.


01:07:30.040 --> 01:07:32.156
Would you like that, sis?


01:07:33.320 --> 01:07:36.278
Are you ok? You're shaking.


01:07:36.920 --> 01:07:38.478
I'm fine.


01:07:46.160 --> 01:07:47.559
Don't you want it?


01:07:47.840 --> 01:07:50.354
I'll take it some other day.


01:07:52.560 --> 01:07:55.438
- It's late. Stay for the night.
- I have to go.


01:07:55.800 --> 01:07:58.872
I'll bring some sheets and
you can sleep on the settee.


01:07:59.040 --> 01:08:01.918
It's hot here,
and someone's waiting for me.


01:08:02.280 --> 01:08:04.475
- Who?
- Someone, in the street.


01:08:05.040 --> 01:08:08.715
- Did you come with someone?
- It's someone I don't know yet,


01:08:08.880 --> 01:08:11.394
someone I'll know tonight
and who'll explain everything.


01:08:11.600 --> 01:08:12.669
Everything?


01:08:13.040 --> 01:08:16.510
I won't find that person here,
or in Barcelona.


01:08:16.680 --> 01:08:18.193
I'd have to go farther.


01:08:19.640 --> 01:08:21.278
Why don't you leave, then?


01:08:23.040 --> 01:08:27.033
I thought you'd leave before
and tell me about it.


01:08:27.280 --> 01:08:28.349
Me?


01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:32.798
Why did you take me
to the train station, then?


01:08:32.960 --> 01:08:35.633
To see other people leave?


01:08:37.040 --> 01:08:39.998
- Are you dating someone?
- No.


01:08:41.040 --> 01:08:43.508
I thought
I'd found someone tonight.


01:08:43.680 --> 01:08:44.669
Who?


01:08:45.840 --> 01:08:48.035
- A very handsome boy.
- What happened?


01:08:48.720 --> 01:08:51.678
I took him home and,
as I fixed the drinks


01:08:51.840 --> 01:08:55.833
and thought of things to say
so as not to go straight to bed,


01:08:56.600 --> 01:08:57.669
he fell asleep.


01:09:05.800 --> 01:09:06.755
What did you do?


01:09:07.800 --> 01:09:08.710
Nothing.


01:09:08.880 --> 01:09:11.713
- You didn't wake him up?
- No.


01:09:26.880 --> 01:09:29.758
- You left him home alone?
- Yes.


01:09:31.080 --> 01:09:32.991
What if he wakes up and you're gone?


01:09:33.160 --> 01:09:36.550
I want to go home
and find him gone.


01:09:37.200 --> 01:09:38.474
What if he's still there?


01:09:38.760 --> 01:09:42.753
Then I'll kill him,
and I'll be in the papers tomorrow,


01:09:43.040 --> 01:09:46.157
then I'll go to jail
and you'll come to visit me.


01:09:46.320 --> 01:09:49.790
Will you visit me in prison?
I think you won't.


01:09:53.840 --> 01:09:56.434
Your hands are beautiful.


01:09:58.240 --> 01:10:00.549
You should have been a pianist.


01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:03.029
Why do you always
change the subject?


01:10:04.680 --> 01:10:08.673
I regret not seeing you operate.


01:10:09.160 --> 01:10:13.153
I'm sorry you married someone
without an imagination.


01:10:13.720 --> 01:10:15.358
We're even.


01:10:15.520 --> 01:10:17.112
No, we're not.


01:10:18.520 --> 01:10:19.919
Come on, come with me.


01:10:20.880 --> 01:10:21.869
Where?


01:10:22.440 --> 01:10:26.433
- Let's go far away tonight.
- I can't go anywhere.


01:10:26.880 --> 01:10:28.518
Pack and let's go.


01:10:28.960 --> 01:10:30.075
And your job?


01:10:30.240 --> 01:10:32.674
Fuck my job. Let's go.


01:10:32.840 --> 01:10:34.751
- I can't.
- Of course you can.


01:10:35.480 --> 01:10:37.436
And leave him here, ill?


01:10:37.760 --> 01:10:39.398
Yes, it's true.


01:10:40.040 --> 01:10:42.190
Now you have to play
the good Samaritan.


01:10:46.360 --> 01:10:48.828
That's my second slap tonight.


01:10:49.640 --> 01:10:51.949
I can tell you've practiced.


01:10:54.560 --> 01:10:57.233
- I've never hit you before, have I?
- No.


01:10:57.560 --> 01:10:59.357
It was the first time.


01:11:01.560 --> 01:11:03.278
Did I hurt you?


01:11:25.160 --> 01:11:27.628
Good night, sis.


01:12:17.600 --> 01:12:19.397
It's too much, isn't it?


01:12:19.920 --> 01:12:20.989
Maybe the eyes.


01:12:21.160 --> 01:12:23.276
- I'll wash it off.
- No, don't.


01:12:24.680 --> 01:12:27.592
- And the dress?
- It's not bad.


01:12:27.960 --> 01:12:28.949
Really?


01:12:29.720 --> 01:12:33.429
- And the wig?
- Not tonight. It's too hot.


01:12:35.520 --> 01:12:37.511
- The lips.
- No, leave them.


01:12:40.400 --> 01:12:41.719
What are you doing?


01:12:42.560 --> 01:12:45.028
- I'll show you how to load it.
- Why?


01:12:45.960 --> 01:12:47.951
Didn't you want to know?


01:12:48.360 --> 01:12:50.157
Is it the guard's gun?


01:12:50.400 --> 01:12:53.392
He lent it to me.
There's no bullets, but it's ok.


01:12:53.840 --> 01:12:55.159
You open it like this.


01:12:56.600 --> 01:12:58.318
You put the bullets in,


01:12:59.560 --> 01:13:00.709
you close it


01:13:04.600 --> 01:13:06.158
and you fire.


01:13:06.760 --> 01:13:08.557
Did the guard show you?


01:13:08.720 --> 01:13:11.393
No. My father and grandfather did.


01:13:11.760 --> 01:13:14.718
- Did they have a gun?
- Because of the reds.


01:13:27.720 --> 01:13:29.711
During the war,
playing on the beach,


01:13:29.880 --> 01:13:32.348
I found a gun in the sand,


01:13:32.520 --> 01:13:34.112
but I couldn't touch it.


01:13:34.280 --> 01:13:37.909
The older boys in the gang
took it away.


01:13:38.640 --> 01:13:40.392
Come on, shoot.


01:13:40.560 --> 01:13:41.959
- Why?
- Come on.


01:13:51.160 --> 01:13:53.754
Promise never to ask for it again.


01:13:54.320 --> 01:13:55.309
Ok.


01:13:56.960 --> 01:13:57.949
All right.


01:14:07.000 --> 01:14:08.479
Will you have your hair cut?


01:14:09.320 --> 01:14:10.150
Yes.


01:14:10.720 --> 01:14:11.709
That's a shame.


01:14:12.280 --> 01:14:13.349
Not for me.


01:14:19.960 --> 01:14:21.598
I met my brother.


01:14:21.800 --> 01:14:24.030
- And?
- He'll come again.


01:14:24.960 --> 01:14:26.109
Really?


01:14:26.880 --> 01:14:30.475
Did I ever tell you that,
as a child, I wanted to be a boy?


01:14:30.720 --> 01:14:33.518
I wanted to be a boy
and my brother a girl.


01:14:33.680 --> 01:14:34.715
Your brother?


01:14:36.160 --> 01:14:37.149
Do you find it strange?


01:14:38.520 --> 01:14:39.270
No.


01:14:39.440 --> 01:14:42.238
We both wanted to be Russians.


01:14:42.880 --> 01:14:43.949
Russians?


01:14:44.800 --> 01:14:47.234
To have a Russian soul, you know.


01:14:47.400 --> 01:14:49.231
Not really.


01:14:50.000 --> 01:14:53.072
Didn't you want to be
from somewhere else, as a kid?


01:14:55.480 --> 01:14:57.357
I don't know, I can't remember.


01:14:57.800 --> 01:14:59.677
What was your ideal age?


01:15:00.240 --> 01:15:01.229
My what?


01:15:01.760 --> 01:15:03.557
The best year you can remember.


01:15:04.480 --> 01:15:06.550
The year the war finished, I guess.


01:15:07.600 --> 01:15:09.318
That's not what I mean.


01:15:10.440 --> 01:15:11.839
What do you mean?


01:15:12.760 --> 01:15:13.954
It doesn't matter.


01:15:19.680 --> 01:15:20.749
What do you think?


01:15:21.760 --> 01:15:23.079
It's nice.


01:15:24.920 --> 01:15:26.273
That's all?


01:15:27.440 --> 01:15:28.714
You look younger.


01:15:28.880 --> 01:15:30.359
Younger than who?


01:15:31.280 --> 01:15:32.110
Than before.


01:15:32.840 --> 01:15:33.829
What do you mean?


01:15:38.520 --> 01:15:41.239
We're not similar at all.


01:15:48.480 --> 01:15:50.948
We never have been.


01:15:54.200 --> 01:15:58.193
It's enough that I dress up,
you don't need to.


01:15:58.480 --> 01:16:00.596
I want to go with you.
Don't go alone.


01:16:00.760 --> 01:16:02.159
I don't mind.


01:16:02.920 --> 01:16:05.514
- You have to practice my signature.
- I know.


01:16:05.680 --> 01:16:07.398
But you don't practice.


01:16:07.680 --> 01:16:08.954
There's still time.


01:16:09.440 --> 01:16:11.237
The government...


01:16:11.400 --> 01:16:14.358
In two months I have to go
to the bank and sign again.


01:16:14.520 --> 01:16:16.078
I've already told you.


01:16:16.760 --> 01:16:19.718
We'll open an account
in a different bank


01:16:19.880 --> 01:16:21.518
and I'll sign.


01:16:22.960 --> 01:16:25.155
So when you leave,


01:16:25.320 --> 01:16:28.790
I can still get your pension.
That's what you wanted, right?


01:16:31.160 --> 01:16:32.878
Did you tell your brother?


01:16:39.880 --> 01:16:40.596
No.


01:16:40.760 --> 01:16:42.512
What did you tell him?


01:16:43.000 --> 01:16:43.989
Nothing.


01:16:46.240 --> 01:16:50.028
And will he want to sign your
death certificate instead of mine?


01:16:50.600 --> 01:16:51.999
I'm sure he will.


01:16:54.440 --> 01:16:56.431
He doesn't like me.


01:16:57.360 --> 01:17:00.158
He doesn't like anyone,
don't worry.


01:17:00.880 --> 01:17:01.676
Where are you going?


01:17:03.560 --> 01:17:04.629
I'm getting changed.


01:17:04.800 --> 01:17:06.791
- No, wait.
- Why?


01:17:08.480 --> 01:17:10.710
- I need to tell you something.
- What?


01:17:13.840 --> 01:17:16.308
- I'm scared to tell you.
- What?


01:17:21.040 --> 01:17:22.837
The Argentinean's baby is mine.


01:17:32.080 --> 01:17:33.069
Yours?


01:17:34.680 --> 01:17:36.750
It was only once,


01:17:37.320 --> 01:17:40.710
the day I was told I had cancer.
You were not here


01:17:41.040 --> 01:17:43.031
and I told her everything.


01:17:43.400 --> 01:17:47.359
- When did you find out?
- She told me tonight.


01:17:49.000 --> 01:17:50.228
What did you say?


01:17:50.880 --> 01:17:52.836
I didn't know what to say.


01:17:53.880 --> 01:17:56.792
- Did she ask for money?
- She doesn't want any.


01:17:56.960 --> 01:17:59.520
- Didn't she ask?
- No, she didn't.


01:18:00.120 --> 01:18:03.829
Did she say if
she'd bring the baby by sometime?


01:18:06.000 --> 01:18:07.638
No, I don't think so.


01:18:16.640 --> 01:18:18.039
Are you upset?


01:18:19.440 --> 01:18:22.955
I also have to tell you something
I've never told you.


01:18:23.240 --> 01:18:25.117
Because I was scared, too.


01:18:27.760 --> 01:18:29.034
Of me?


01:18:29.200 --> 01:18:30.269
Yes.


01:18:31.040 --> 01:18:32.439
What is it?


01:18:34.280 --> 01:18:37.352
My brother isn't my brother,
he's my son.


01:18:39.360 --> 01:18:40.554
I don't understand.


01:18:41.160 --> 01:18:42.912
I had him with my father.


01:18:57.920 --> 01:19:01.708
He didn't make me do it,
I did it because I wanted to.


01:19:02.560 --> 01:19:04.118
But you were very young.


01:19:04.280 --> 01:19:06.919
He was the only one I loved.


01:19:09.880 --> 01:19:11.472
Does Santi know?


01:19:13.120 --> 01:19:14.917
I think so.


01:19:15.560 --> 01:19:17.915
Anyway, I gave him my diary.


01:19:18.520 --> 01:19:20.715
That's why you never showed me?


01:19:20.880 --> 01:19:23.792
The diary?
You never asked.


01:19:24.360 --> 01:19:28.035
Once you said you would,
but you didn't.


01:19:28.280 --> 01:19:29.315
Really?


01:19:29.480 --> 01:19:30.754
Can't you remember?


01:19:31.120 --> 01:19:33.111
I'll give to you, if you want.


01:19:38.360 --> 01:19:40.920
I want to give you something too.


01:19:50.440 --> 01:19:51.839
This guide.


01:19:52.720 --> 01:19:54.312
It's very old.


01:19:55.840 --> 01:19:59.833
One of my first jobs
was to help make it.


01:20:05.080 --> 01:20:07.036
Why is it underlined?


01:20:07.720 --> 01:20:10.837
One very hot summer
I collected payments,


01:20:11.760 --> 01:20:15.355
and I marked
all the shaded streets.


01:20:16.400 --> 01:20:19.597
I thought the next summer
I'd go faster


01:20:19.760 --> 01:20:21.716
and wouldn't be as hot.


01:20:22.640 --> 01:20:26.235
But it wasn't much use,
I soon started working at the 0pera.


01:20:28.400 --> 01:20:31.119
It's like a big map of shadows.


01:20:31.360 --> 01:20:33.555
Passeig de Gràcia is not there.


01:20:35.000 --> 01:20:36.399
I know.


01:20:36.680 --> 01:20:39.558
I tore off all the pages
where you could see it.


01:20:42.120 --> 01:20:44.190
These clothes are too warm.


01:20:44.800 --> 01:20:46.358
And the shoes are tight.


01:20:46.520 --> 01:20:48.875
- I'll take them to the cobbler.
- He closed down.


01:20:49.440 --> 01:20:51.237
I'll find another one.


01:20:52.440 --> 01:20:56.115
- My grandfather was a cobbler.
- I know. You told me.


01:20:57.000 --> 01:20:59.309
- Do you know how he died?
- How?


01:21:00.880 --> 01:21:01.949
Burnt.


01:21:04.240 --> 01:21:05.229
Burnt?


01:21:08.120 --> 01:21:11.590
0ne night, as he was sleeping
beside my grandmother,


01:21:11.760 --> 01:21:13.113
he started to burn.


01:21:14.720 --> 01:21:16.199
What do you mean?


01:21:16.360 --> 01:21:19.511
His body started burning.


01:21:19.680 --> 01:21:21.910
It's called spontaneous combustion.


01:21:22.080 --> 01:21:25.436
That's impossible.
Nobody sets on fire spontaneously.


01:21:25.760 --> 01:21:28.228
He was fatter than me,
and drank.


01:21:28.640 --> 01:21:30.870
You haven't drunk in ages.


01:21:31.040 --> 01:21:32.996
Besides, it's impossible.


01:21:33.240 --> 01:21:35.071
Nobody sets on fire like that.


01:21:35.240 --> 01:21:36.832
It's possible.


01:21:39.200 --> 01:21:41.077
I know how to do it.


01:21:41.960 --> 01:21:43.029
What?


01:21:44.440 --> 01:21:47.398
Burning something
without touching it.


01:21:50.040 --> 01:21:51.917
I can burn things, if I like.


01:21:52.080 --> 01:21:53.195
You can?


01:21:54.000 --> 01:21:54.716
Yes.


01:21:56.640 --> 01:21:57.789
How?


01:21:59.240 --> 01:22:00.798
Just thinking about it.


01:22:02.160 --> 01:22:03.878
Thinking about it?


01:22:08.080 --> 01:22:08.671
Look.


01:22:08.840 --> 01:22:10.796
Can you see the handkerchief?


01:22:10.960 --> 01:22:13.952
I've been thinking about it
getting warm for a while.


01:22:14.520 --> 01:22:17.478
It will start burning
at some point.


01:22:17.960 --> 01:22:20.918
- Are you serious?
- Yes.


01:22:25.480 --> 01:22:27.072
No, don't touch it!


01:22:27.520 --> 01:22:29.556
It doesn't seem to be burning.


01:22:30.240 --> 01:22:32.708
It's hard, because it's damp.


01:22:33.200 --> 01:22:36.112
And I'm out of practice,
I haven't tried in ages.


01:22:36.640 --> 01:22:38.312
Have you ever burnt anything?


01:22:40.680 --> 01:22:41.476
What?


01:22:42.360 --> 01:22:45.557
At first it was only little things,
until one day


01:22:46.120 --> 01:22:49.510
I wanted to see if I could
burn something bigger.


01:22:49.960 --> 01:22:51.916
I got scared and stopped.


01:22:52.360 --> 01:22:53.839
What did you burn?


01:22:55.280 --> 01:22:56.156
The Opera House.


01:22:56.440 --> 01:22:57.395
What?


01:22:57.760 --> 01:22:59.318
I burnt the Opera House.


01:22:59.920 --> 01:23:01.911
You're kidding, aren't you?


01:23:02.600 --> 01:23:05.034
Do you actually think you burnt it?


01:23:05.200 --> 01:23:07.555
Yes, I did.


01:23:07.720 --> 01:23:09.199
You were at home, then.


01:23:10.520 --> 01:23:12.397
I did it from here.


01:23:31.200 --> 01:23:34.237
- It was burning earlier, right?
- No.


01:23:34.520 --> 01:23:37.751
- How did it set on fire?
- I told you. It's me.


01:23:37.920 --> 01:23:39.353
With your mind?


01:23:41.560 --> 01:23:44.597
- Did you burn it like that?
- Yes.


01:23:45.400 --> 01:23:47.834
But it was harder, it's farther.


01:23:48.120 --> 01:23:50.111
Why did you burn it?


01:23:52.200 --> 01:23:55.670
Everybody said
we needed a new Opera House.


01:23:56.120 --> 01:23:59.351
More and more people started saying
they wished it'd burnt down


01:23:59.520 --> 01:24:02.080
so they could build
a newer, bigger one.


01:24:03.280 --> 01:24:05.271
So eventually, I did it.


01:24:06.320 --> 01:24:07.912
I burnt it.


01:24:08.440 --> 01:24:10.192
Have you ever told anyone?


01:24:11.280 --> 01:24:12.269
No, I haven't.


01:24:12.760 --> 01:24:14.352
I was scared of telling.


01:24:14.640 --> 01:24:16.073
Even me?


01:24:18.000 --> 01:24:19.399
Especially you.


01:24:26.480 --> 01:24:28.516
We forgot about the opera.


01:24:29.240 --> 01:24:31.117
It must be almost over.


01:24:40.600 --> 01:24:43.433
What you said about Callas
is true, isn't it?


01:24:45.320 --> 01:24:46.594
Of course it is.


01:24:47.080 --> 01:24:49.071
What did she say
when you brought her dog back?


01:24:50.080 --> 01:24:53.197
She thanked me.
I told you, didn't I?


01:24:53.520 --> 01:24:54.635
That's all?


01:24:54.800 --> 01:24:57.872
She was in a hurry and
just thanked me.


01:24:58.280 --> 01:24:59.429
In Italian?


01:24:59.600 --> 01:25:02.558
Yes, in Italian.


01:25:04.240 --> 01:25:06.435
<i>"Ti ringrazio."</i>


01:25:14.400 --> 01:25:15.719
I'm sorry.


01:25:20.560 --> 01:25:22.676
Have you taken all your tablets?


01:25:28.600 --> 01:25:30.192
Aren't you tired?


01:25:31.560 --> 01:25:33.039
Not yet.


01:25:34.040 --> 01:25:36.190
- And you?
- No, not yet.


01:25:38.680 --> 01:25:40.989
It's very hot tonight, isn't it?


01:25:42.360 --> 01:25:44.316
Do you need to go to the toilet?


01:25:44.760 --> 01:25:45.636
Yes.


01:25:47.120 --> 01:25:49.509
Go first, if you like.


01:25:50.840 --> 01:25:52.432
Are you sure?


01:25:53.280 --> 01:25:54.679
I'll wait.


01:26:00.240 --> 01:26:01.559
I won't be long.


01:26:06.560 --> 01:26:07.993
Are you going like that?


01:26:09.160 --> 01:26:11.628
It's very late.
They'll be sleeping.


01:27:58.640 --> 01:28:02.189
With Castilian loyalty
I'm proud to state


01:28:02.360 --> 01:28:05.989
that 40 years of progressive
dehispanicisation


01:28:06.160 --> 01:28:09.357
calls for an immediate
and continuous effort


01:28:09.520 --> 01:28:11.317
in the opposite direction


01:28:11.480 --> 01:28:14.153
to rehispanicise Catalonia,


01:28:14.560 --> 01:28:17.518
into which I hope to put
all my efforts,


01:28:17.680 --> 01:28:21.070
from kindergarten
to highest cultural levels,


01:28:21.440 --> 01:28:25.319
the only real explanation
of many regretful


01:28:25.600 --> 01:28:27.670
events and attitudes,


01:28:27.840 --> 01:28:30.149
even in the seemingly farthest


01:28:30.320 --> 01:28:33.118
areas of the spiritual sphere...

